# ref-9e5a4cd-body-churn
# A box stack settling to sleep beside a kinematic plate. The plate's fat bounds
# overlap the top box without touching, so a non-touching contact persists across the
# stack's sleep cycle -- the exact case the encoded body-sim locator (9e5a4cd) has to
# fix up on the sleep path. The harness vocabulary has no explicit destroy/wake
# directive, so the churn is exercised through sleep, which nulls and restores the
# encoded sim indices.
# Reference: vanilla float box3d at upstream commit 9e5a4cd.
# Fixed: fixed3d on this branch (encoded body-sim index + fatAABB split ported).
# Observable: the stack settles to a stable pile; the encoded index encoding is pure
#   integer bookkeeping and does not move body trajectories, so the fixed and float
#   traces agree inside the usual tolerance.
# Tolerance: pos 0.007 rot 0.001 vel 0.03, counts exact (10 bodies: 1 static, 3 dynamic
#   stack, 1 kinematic plate = 5; keep 6 to allow one extra contact or an awake-count
#   skew from sleep timing). Resting height of the top box within 0.05 m.
expect pos 0.007 rot 0.001 vel 0.03 horizon 120 counts 10
world gravity 0 -10 0 dt 1 60 substeps 4 steps 180
body static position 0 -0.5 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body dynamic position 0 0.5 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body dynamic position 0 1.5 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body dynamic position 0 2.5 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body kinematic position 1.04 2.5 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
shape 0 box 5 0.5 5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
shape 1 box 0.5 0.5 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
shape 2 box 0.5 0.5 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
shape 3 box 0.5 0.5 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
shape 4 box 0.5 0.5 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
